  "findings": [
    "Where a sitemap is declared, a handful of requests lists 97 to 4954 product URLs; the home page links to 0 to 20.",
    "allbirds.com links no product URL in its static home page HTML (rendered navigation); its sitemaps list 692.",
    "Sitemaps lag the storefront: 2 of 45 home-page products (seasonal bundles) were not yet listed, so sitemap discovery complements link discovery rather than replacing it.",
    "rothys.com robots.txt on www declares a sitemap on the bare host: cross-host declaration is normal and must not be dropped.",
    "No sampled sitemap carried lastmod, so recency cannot be read from these sitemaps.",
    "books.toscrape.com declares no sitemap and its product paths (/catalogue/) fall outside the product rule: the rule undercounts, never overcounts, such sites."
  ],
  "decision": {
    "knowledge": "INDEPENDENT_NATIVE",
    "native": [
      "adapter/web/src/robots.rs::sitemaps",
      "adapter/web/src/sitemap.rs::parse"
    ],
    "validated": "the native parser reads 9, 2477 and 181 entries from captured gymshark.com and rothys.com sitemaps, equal to their <loc> element counts, with no image:loc entry",
    "runtime": "wired: the web provider reads XML responses only as sitemaps (source type PUBLIC_SITEMAP_XML, no products asserted, entries as links) and reports the sitemaps the origin's robots.txt declares; a research crawl enqueues those from depth-0 seeds and index children at priority 95, each URL still leased, robots-checked and inside the depth and URL budget. Not exercised live from the development sandbox, whose network blocks the provider's direct connections."
  },
  "limits": "five sites, one capture time, six sitemaps per site, a path rule for product URLs; catalogue completeness of sitemaps was not measured"
}
